Subject: Build without the health-report service and Normandy
Reason: MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT and MOZ_NORMANDY are project_flag()s that can
 only be set by imply_option() in browser/moz.configure (mozconfig/env is
 rejected). Turning them off, together with MOZ_TELEMETRY_REPORTING unset and
 --disable-crashreporter, also leaves MOZ_DATA_REPORTING undefined, which
 removes the data-submission policy, its first-run notification and the
 Normandy startup hook / about:studies. Prefs can only disable these at run
 time; this removes them from the build.
Owner: privacy
---
diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -3,11 +3,13 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
 imply_option("MOZ_PLACES", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT", True)
+# Amaya: no Firefox Health Report / data-submission service.
+imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT", False)
 imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_SYNC", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEDICATED_PROFILES", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_BLOCK_PROFILE_DOWNGRADE", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
+# Amaya: no Normandy recipe runner (remote pref/add-on studies).
+imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", False)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
